      "message": "The logic looks good to me. I just had one question. Does the SMP support require that all of these properties exist on D-Bus?\n\nFor example, if an SMP system did not implement Enabled on the chassis, or it did not use the applications that provide the PowerSystemInputs interfaces, then the D-Bus getProperty calls will fail. This will cause the chassis to be skipped.\n\nIs that OK? If not, you may need to distinguish between \"expected\" D-Bus failures (property/interface does not exist) vs. \"unexpected\" ones.\n\nAnother option is to use compile flags or a JSON data file to turn on/off checking for certain properties.",
